WEBVTT

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.940
The three of us are finally 
going to be working together!

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.730
I'm so excited!

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:10.320
Come on, Uki! Let's go to club!

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.360
Huh? I'm not going.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.400
You're already skipping? 
Uki, you delinquent!

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.870
Hey! Don't say it like that!

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:19.450
What's the matter?

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.620
Arima-san!

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.260
Let's go to club!

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:27.080
Proficiency tests are coming up, 
so we're putting club activities on hold.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:31.610
What?! But we finally got three members!

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:45.020
<b>Anima Yell!</b>

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:06.430
<b>Episode 3: The Cheer Association, 
Cheering for Love!</b>

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:06.430
There's more to cheer than club activities.

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:11.440
Academics is another important field 
that cheerleaders should concentrate on.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.440
It's essential to cheer.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:20.110
<i>Thank goodness. Kohane has no 
idea what's going on, either.</i>

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:24.160
In America, where cheerleading hails 
from, cheerleaders are admired

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.120
by all and considered to be top-class women.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.960
They are proper, intelligent,

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:32.010
beautiful, with sparkling smiles,

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:34.250
and have the ability to be 
 motivational leaders.

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.920
<i>She did her best...</i>

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.500
I'm not saying we have to go that far,

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:43.380
but it doesn't hurt to have good grades.

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:46.090
Speaking of, how are your overall grades?

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.930
<b>Below average                                Above average</b>

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:49.520
Then we need to train.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:55.150
<b>Entered School as an Elite</b>

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:55.150
Let us work together to lift Hatoya-san up!

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:56.020
Yeah!

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:58.860
<i>Arima-san, you're good!</i>

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.410
Let's start with English.

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:03.390
I hate English.

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:05.680
All you did was open your textbook.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:08.160
Most cheer calls are in English.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:11.450
Audiences might understand your cheers 
better if you understand English.

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:12.880
Oh, yeah!

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:14.130
<i>She's so close.</i>

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:17.740
Like, "Go to wah!" Right?

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:20.130
It's actually "go for win."

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:23.770
There's more to this than just being loud.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:26.250
You could damage your throat that way.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:32.810
The trick to doing proper calls is to 
call from deep down within your stomach.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:33.850
Like this?

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:35.100
What happened to English?

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:38.940
Japanese History

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.940
It's easiest to learn history by writing it down.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.970
I hate it.

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:48.200
Fight!!

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.090
What are you even trying to learn?!

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:47.820
My hand has a mind of its own.

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:49.560
<b>Math I</b>

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:52.750
<i>You probably can't work cheer into math...</i>

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:53.750
Hey!

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:56.400
Seriously! What are you drawing?!

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.140
Squee.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:03.070
Cheer power... I lack cheer power...

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:05.930
Even after you kept forcing 
cheer into everything...

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:08.040
You leave me no choice.

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:12.690
What?!

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:15.690
Go, go, Hatoya! Let's go, Hatoya!

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:17.190
Go, fight, win!

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:20.270
Go, go, Hatoya! Let's go, Hatoya!

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.540
Now I'm overflowing with cheer power!

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:21.780
Go, fight, win!

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:22.440
Shut up!

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:26.880
Also, that outfit? Did you 
forget we didn't have club?

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.080
O-O-O-Of course I didn't...

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:32.750
Now I have to return all that cheer power!

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:34.620
How about you put it toward your studies?

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:37.420
I'll be done in a jiffy.

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:43.380
Ta-da!

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:46.270
The super awesome shorts 
I got from Arima-san!

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:49.680
They give you the amazing ability 
to cheer with just your butt!

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:52.270
That's not what those were made for!

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:54.520
<b>The Next Day</b>

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:57.270
So... What subject should we work on today?

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.820
U-Um...

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:03.500
I'll study on my own today!

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:05.490
You mustn't run away!

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:07.530
I don't think she's trying to run away.

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:10.440
I think she's worried that we 
might not be able to study.

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:11.770
So she's worried about us?

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:12.660
Yeah.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:17.390
If that's the case, I'd feel much better

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:20.760
if you'd study where we can see you.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:23.010
True...

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:25.010
I'm sorry.

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:28.560
It's fine. You're the one 
doing the hard work here.

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:32.060
But I think you should 
be studying every day.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:34.170
It's harder to learn when 
you don't stick with it.

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:37.020
Well, when your grades are good, 
the teachers remember you more,

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:39.880
plus it's easier to find an advisor.

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:47.260
I sense a sudden and drastic change...

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:48.980
Y-Yeah...

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:52.550
You need to remember to take breaks, too.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:55.500
Go for win!

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.290
That's not an answer!

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.170
<b>The Next Day</b>

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:04.670
She's even studying during her break?

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:08.180
She seems to be trying hard 
not to bring up cheer, too.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:10.980
After she kept saying "cheer" all the time...

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:19.130
Now that I've gotten into it, 
studying is so much fun!

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:20.980
I don't care about cheer anymore!

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:23.020
Anymore... anymore...

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:26.120
And then I'll be all alone again...

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:29.530
I think your trauma switch flips 
on a little too easily!

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:33.980
Studying while you're walking is dangerous.

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:37.720
With my grades, I have to 
study on my way home, too.

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:41.170
<i>I mean, it's nice that she's not 
doing anything crazy, but...</i>

00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:50.170
<i>Kohane would usually be like...</i>

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:51.840
<i>"I'll hold your stuff for you!"</i>

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:52.730
Koha—

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:54.580
Pardon me...

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:58.850
I've never been in this area 
before, and I think I'm lost.

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.680
I'd like to go here.

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:04.630
Oh, sure. To go here...

00:07:05.170 --> 00:07:06.480
I'll take you there!

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:09.580
Oh, great! Thank you so much.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:15.100
Thank you for your help.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.840
Bye-bye!

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:22.700
Kohane! What's wrong? Do you feel sick?

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:25.960
I-I'm trying to make sure the stuff
I learned doesn't spill out...

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:27.210
Physically?!

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:32.840
But I'm relieved. You're acting 
like the Kohane I know.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:34.400
But this isn't good!

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:38.330
If my grades don't improve, 
we might not find an advisor!

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:40.620
That's what you were worried about?

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:44.800
We were just talking about 
that as a possibility...

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:46.860
Sorry.

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:50.200
But if you kept acting weird like that,

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:53.240
it probably would've thrown 
me off and affected my grades.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:55.870
Arima-san's on the brink, to be honest.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:56.740
Weird?!

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:00.500
You just need to keep being the usual Kohane.

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:02.480
But I want perfect scores...

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:04.670
You were planning on 
getting perfect scores?!

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:07.720
Just leave that to Arima-san.

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:09.930
I see...

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:16.140
My shoulders feel a bit lighter now.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.020
<i>Bye-bye, cheer!</i>

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:29.440
It looks like Hatoya-san's calmed down.

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:30.150
Yeah.

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:34.010
She was definitely pushing herself, 
so this is probably for the best.

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:37.320
<i>Arima-san is really good 
at reading emotions...</i>

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:38.620
However...

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:41.750
The timing is pretty bad.

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:45.500
Proficiency Test
First Period  Math I
Second Period  Communication English I
Third Period  Basic Chemistry
Fourth Period  Japanese History B

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:45.050
Yeah, our tests do start today.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:47.250
<b>A few days later</b>

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:49.000
All right. That's it for today.

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:53.160
Uki, Uki, let's go!

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:56.590
The three of us are finally 
going to start our club!

00:08:56.590 --> 00:09:00.470
Yes. Let's go... take your supplementary exam.

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:02.860
U-Uki!

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:05.560
You can do it. I'll be cheering you on.

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:08.980
But I'm the one who wants to cheer!

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:14.160
I'm finally free...

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:15.150
Good work.

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:17.790
So what are we going to do?

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:20.160
The first thing you need to do is stretch.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:23.480
We need to take time to 
work on your flexibility

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:25.840
so you don't get hurt.

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:29.540
Meanwhile, Sawatari-san will be 
practicing the starting position.

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:33.320
First, put your hands on your hips 
so that your arms form triangles.

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:35.920
Stick out your chest, 
and lift up your chin slightly.

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:37.930
This is the basic stance.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:40.460
While in that position, put your strength

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:42.620
into your abs and stand tall.

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:50.060
By the way, I see you're both 
in your practice clothes.

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:54.320
Arima-san gave me these!

00:09:54.680 --> 00:09:57.930
I see. So those are Arima-san's clothes.

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:02.650
Okay! I'm done with all my stretches!

00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:04.720
I wanna do the starting position, too!

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:06.250
Um...

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:10.290
The basketball club is 
going to be using this area.

00:10:10.730 --> 00:10:13.870
Each club should have designated areas.

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:15.470
What club are you guys in?

00:10:15.470 --> 00:10:17.510
U-Um...

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:20.090
The cheer club... we hope... ma'am!

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:21.790
Wait, what?

00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:24.300
The cheer club... we hope... ma'am!

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:26.270
<i>Does she think that actually helped?</i>

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:27.980
Whatever. We'll be using this area.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:30.850
Please! Let us use this area, too!

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:33.770
We'll cheer you on! Come on, Uki!

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:35.110
Come on! You'll just be in the way!

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:41.240
<i>We only know the starting position!</i>

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:45.850
I guess we didn't think about 
where we could practice.

00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:47.620
We can check some places out.

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:55.840
This area's filled with sports clubs.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:59.190
I wonder if they'd let us use some corner...

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:01.960
I'll hold this end for you.

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:03.600
Uh, who are you?

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:08.220
We're probably better off if there 
aren't other people around.

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:10.020
Yeah, I completely agree.

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:11.960
There...

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:12.970
Make sure you stretch...

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:15.320
This place is pretty packed today, too.

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:18.070
The only place left is...

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:26.440
If you guys are okay with me only 
working in this spot right here...

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:27.450
That's too small!

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:31.900
Maybe we can't get a practice area 
if we aren't an official club.

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.410
Social stratification...

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:40.520
Perfect timing, Inukai-sensei!

00:11:42.070 --> 00:11:44.220
A place to do your club activities?

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:47.600
Well, the areas are assigned 
depending on what club you're in.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:52.350
U-Um... Could we be considered 
a club with just three members?

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:57.150
I mean, we have three out of five 
people! That's close enough, right?

00:11:57.150 --> 00:12:00.380
If we round it off, it'd be five! Right, Sensei?

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:02.610
Actually, if you round off 
three, it'd be zero...

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:05.270
Three...

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:08.990
Congratulations on three members!

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:13.040
Why are you walking around with that?!

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:15.130
Congratulations?

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:18.600
With three members, 
you can be an association.

00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:23.880
Wh-What's an association?

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:26.490
You can be considered an 
association with three people.

00:12:26.490 --> 00:12:28.320
You don't get funding or a club room,

00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:30.420
but you'll be given a place 
to do your activities.

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:35.280
We'll establish that nao!

00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:36.460
Sure thing.

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:39.400
Let's see... the space that's 
available right now is...

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:41.320
We'd like a space in the gym, if possible.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:43.700
Yeah, not happening. 
No way there'll be space.

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:47.450
Oh, it looks like the roof 
is open on some days.

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:48.950
No!

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:51.830
Apparently this old AV room is open.

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:56.140
Wow, this is amazing! It's so big!

00:12:56.140 --> 00:13:00.380
The ceiling is a little low, 
but this should work for a while.

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:01.790
This is a great room.

00:13:01.790 --> 00:13:03.840
Why isn't anyone else using it?

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:07.850
Well, that's because you can 
hear the sounds of the piano

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:10.200
from the old music room below at night...

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:11.470
So it's a stigmatized property!

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:14.680
We can't, we can't, we can't!
No, no, no! No way!

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:16.140
It'll be fine, Uki.

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:18.430
<i>Your words aren't reassuring at all!</i>

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:20.190
That's rather unrealistic.

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:23.530
It's probably a patrolling 
teacher sneaking in to play it.

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:24.950
<i>And she doesn't believe in ghosts!</i>

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:28.640
We'll be fine. Apparently, 
it only comes around at night.

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:30.750
That's not the point!

00:13:31.650 --> 00:13:32.700
Uki.

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:35.080
Let's just go to the roof, then.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:37.460
Huh? But, Kohane...

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:40.190
I'll just keep my eyes 
closed and do my best.

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:41.960
This place is fine!

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:46.060
Okay, let's have you fill out the paperwork 
to make your association official.

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:48.160
<i>And she pulled something 
out of nowhere again.</i>

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:51.870
<i>Sensei... She's done so much for us...</i>

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:54.360
<i>I want to express how thankful I am!</i>

00:13:55.280 --> 00:13:56.850
Thank you very much!

00:13:57.200 --> 00:13:58.100
You got it!

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:00.730
Association Name

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:04.030
One, two, three, four, 
five, six, seven, eight!

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:07.210
One, two, three, four, 
five, six, seven, eight!

00:14:07.210 --> 00:14:10.510
One, two, three, four, 
five, six, seven, eight!

00:14:10.510 --> 00:14:13.710
One, two, three, four, 
five, six, seven, eight!

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:17.240
One, two, three, four, 
five, six, seven, eight!

00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:20.790
We're finally starting to 
look like cheerleaders.

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:25.170
I wanna hurry up and cheer for someone.

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:27.960
You should probably cheer 
for yourself first.

00:14:27.960 --> 00:14:29.050
Oh, yeah!

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:33.180
<b>Cheer Association
</b>We'll cheer you on!
Looking for requests
 and new recruits

00:14:29.520 --> 00:14:31.240
Ta-da! Look at this!

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:33.180
I made us a poster!

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:37.800
I see. Since we're an association, 
we're allowed to put up posters.

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:39.270
You sure work fast.

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:43.020
<b>Bulletin Board
Volleyball Club | Soccer Club | Drama Club
Light Music Club | Cheer Association</b>

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:42.090
I already put them up on all the 
bulletin boards in the school!

00:14:42.090 --> 00:14:43.290
You really do work fast!

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:46.400
I also made sure to throw one into 
the old music room downstairs, too.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:48.040
Why would you do that?!

00:14:48.040 --> 00:14:51.630
Maybe ghostie-chan will want to join, too!

00:14:51.630 --> 00:14:53.410
How stupid are you?!

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:56.670
Indeed. Ghosts don't exist.

00:14:56.670 --> 00:14:57.900
Yeah, yeah!

00:14:57.900 --> 00:15:01.950
And even if they were to join, 
our kicks would never line up.

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:03.930
Ghosts don't have legs, after all.

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:07.820
It'd be difficult to hold their 
legs during stunts, as well.

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:08.840
Oh, yeah!

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:09.720
You took it seriously?

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:13.350
That's not the problem here!
We need to be more serious!

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:18.000
If we get too involved with stuff 
like that, they might even possess us!

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:20.580
You know a lot, for someone 
who can't stand this stuff.

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:21.730
A long time ago...

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:27.840
I researched everything about it 
to find out why I was so scared.

00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:32.490
And now she knows even more about 
it, making her even more scared.

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:34.720
Of course I could never 
really understand it!

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:36.620
My old self should've figured that out!

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:40.000
But we really can hear the 
piano from time to time.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:41.000
Right?!

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.630
Not to mention, I can feel 
someone's eyes on us.

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:46.880
I swear someone's staring right at us...

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:48.380
Like right now!

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:52.990
There's no one here.

00:15:52.990 --> 00:15:55.470
I'm pretty sure I felt someone's presence...

00:15:56.980 --> 00:15:57.770
Um...

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:01.400
We came here because of your poster.

00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:03.480
Akitsune-san! Tatejima-san!

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:05.370
Do you know them?

00:16:05.370 --> 00:16:07.290
Yeah! They're in my class.

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:08.480
Right, Uki?

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:10.480
Y-Yeah...

00:16:10.480 --> 00:16:13.320
They... They have legs, right?

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:16.450
<b>Cheer Association</b>

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:16.450
I figured you'd be one of the 
ones doing this, Hatoya-san.

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:19.700
Yeah! Did you need some cheering? 
Or did you want to join?

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:23.830
I wanted you to cheer me on so I can 
tell the person I like how I feel!

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:25.990
H-How you feel?

00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:29.630
<i>That's not what cheerleading is for...</i>

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:30.510
<i>But...</i>

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:33.850
<i>I'll do anything that'll 
help people out, peep!</i>

00:16:33.850 --> 00:16:35.840
<i>I wouldn't be surprised if 
Hatoya-san went along with it.</i>

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:42.230
Well, um... I don't really understand 
stuff like love very much...

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:45.640
You'll just be cheering me 
on. It's not a big deal.

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:52.990
<b>Desire to help</b>

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:52.990
<b>Can't</b>

00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:49.000
Was I asking for too much?

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:52.540
Should it have been something club-related?

00:16:54.100 --> 00:16:56.480
I'll do it! I'll cheer you on!

00:16:56.480 --> 00:16:58.240
<i>Is this cheer power?</i>

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:02.110
But this isn't what cheering for 
a confession looks like, right?

00:17:02.110 --> 00:17:05.250
Actually, I was wondering 
if you'd hear me out, too.

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:09.090
<b>Her first time,                       A beginner, but she's             Experienced, and can
but she's athletic                   super enthusiastic                 teach various things</b>

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:08.260
This is how it looks regarding cheer.

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:14.880
<b>Absolutely no experience</b>

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:11.990
As for love and relationships, it'd be this.

00:17:12.720 --> 00:17:14.880
Even so, please...

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:17.640
So, what's this person like?

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:20.810
Smart! The person's my PT, after all!

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:22.680
Yeah, they definitely sound smart.

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:24.240
Yeah.

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:25.280
<i>PT?</i>

00:17:25.280 --> 00:17:27.060
*Peepity tweet.*

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:28.970
Does that mean they're older?

00:17:28.970 --> 00:17:30.690
Yeah, a sophomore in college.

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:32.440
*Peepity tweet.*

00:17:32.760 --> 00:17:34.570
Wow, they're an adult!

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:36.400
That four-year age gap is huge.

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:41.180
They're in college, so that means 
seminars, part-time jobs, mixers...

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:43.360
They're always looking to meet someone.

00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:45.100
Don't make her more uneasy.

00:17:45.100 --> 00:17:47.870
No, I'm talking about my older brother.

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:49.380
<b>Older Brother</b>

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:49.380
Get a grip, bro!

00:17:49.930 --> 00:17:52.250
If they don't have someone 
they already like,

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:54.630
this might be the best time to approach them.

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:57.800
They say that soldiers honor swiftness.

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:59.190
Soldiers?

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:03.500
But wouldn't you already be at an advantage 
since students and PT, or rather,

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:05.040
private tutors, tend to be close?

00:18:05.040 --> 00:18:07.130
What are you doing back there?

00:18:07.130 --> 00:18:09.650
I don't know what to say, 
so I thought I'd at least cheer.

00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:14.530
Hey, don't they say the fastest way to 
someone's heart is through their stomach?

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:17.840
I see! So you have to strengthen 
your grip strength and bam!

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:19.320
I didn't mean literally...

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:22.280
Oh, I've actually tried that before...

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:24.960
But they ended up stuck 
in bed the next day.

00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:26.890
"Feels like my stomach's being 
twisted around," they said...

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:29.250
<i>So she did actually grab 
their stomach, literally!</i>

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:33.920
I know! Why don't you try telling 
them how you feel with a cheer?

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:35.060
With a cheer?

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:40.760
Mouse Transport

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:39.720
All right, any questions so far?

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:40.760
Yeah!

00:18:41.020 --> 00:18:43.390
I love you!

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:46.060
No thank you!

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:49.640
They say when you want to tell someone

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:52.450
how you feel, the setting is important.

00:18:52.450 --> 00:18:55.730
I hear it might go better 
between dusk and nighttime.

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:58.830
Oh, and the first three 
months is the best time!

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:00.590
Why not put yourself in an extreme situation

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:02.740
so that the suspension 
bridge effect might occur?

00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:05.990
That sort of sounds scary coming from you.

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:09.360
I know! You should definitely 
wear your uniform!

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:10.870
You mean, like, dress to impress?

00:19:11.180 --> 00:19:13.900
"Just the fact that they're high 
school girls makes them precious."

00:19:13.900 --> 00:19:15.600
That's what my brother says.

00:19:15.600 --> 00:19:18.510
Arima-san, let's forget about your brother.

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:22.220
What's most important is 
to tell them how you feel.

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:24.440
With the best smile!

00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:27.930
And hopefully you'll be able to 
become boyfriend and girlfriend.

00:19:28.410 --> 00:19:30.740
An older boyfriend, huh?

00:19:32.340 --> 00:19:34.090
Uh...

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:36.690
You've got the wrong idea.

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:42.820
Um... This tutor is...

00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:47.200
a girl.

00:19:56.960 --> 00:20:00.920
Then whatever Arima-san's brother 
said might not help that much.

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:01.630
Huh?

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:06.260
Uh, I'm not sure how much his opinions 
would've helped with a guy, either.

00:20:06.660 --> 00:20:09.030
Um... Well...

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:11.260
Are you sure?

00:20:11.930 --> 00:20:13.850
Of course!

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:18.150
I think the fact that you can fall 
in love with anyone is great!

00:20:18.600 --> 00:20:22.470
I don't understand love and 
relationships, but I know that much.

00:20:26.150 --> 00:20:27.300
Thanks!

00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:34.290
Hatoya-san is amazing.

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:39.400
I couldn't even think of 
what to say. I'm useless.

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:41.100
That's not true.

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:43.300
I-I accidentally said that out loud.

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:45.080
The reason you couldn't say anything

00:20:45.080 --> 00:20:47.260
is because you care about your friend

00:20:47.880 --> 00:20:51.310
and couldn't say anything lightly.

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:53.700
But that means you're thinking hard about it.

00:20:55.860 --> 00:20:58.810
<i>Now I feel like I'm being cheered on, too.</i>

00:20:58.810 --> 00:21:01.590
<i>Wait, did I sound like some know-it-all?</i>

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:04.320
<b>A Few Days Later</b>

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:07.200
It worked!

00:21:08.180 --> 00:21:09.850
Good for you!

00:21:09.850 --> 00:21:12.330
The Arima method worked!

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:13.450
The Arima method?

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:19.000
I told her how I felt while 
I was still wearing my uniform.

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:20.210
"I like you."

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:23.900
Does this mean that my brother was right?

00:21:23.900 --> 00:21:25.970
No... Or I guess he was...

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:30.600
This really made me realize 
how great cheer is.

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:33.720
D-Does that mean you want to give it a try?

00:21:33.720 --> 00:21:35.850
Hmm... Maybe.

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:38.190
Then... Then fill out this form!

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:38.860
<b>Club Application
Club name (Association name)
Class | Name</b>

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:41.860
Oh, but I decided to join the home ec club.

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:43.740
I'm gonna make her a 
delicious meal next time!

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:46.750
Thanks for everything!

00:21:46.750 --> 00:21:50.640
If we'd acted a little sooner, 
they might've joined.

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:51.980
Too bad.

00:21:51.980 --> 00:21:56.460
But I'm glad the first cheer from 
the cheer association went well!

00:21:56.460 --> 00:21:57.330
Indeed.

00:21:57.710 --> 00:22:00.340
I wonder what I should cook first...

00:23:38.850 --> 00:23:41.180
Next time: "Let's Cheer Up!"
